YOUR MISSION
Build a production-oriented Docker image for a small Go HTTP service. Compare a single-stage image with a multi-stage image,
run the app as a non-root user, and prove the image-size reduction with real measurements.
Learning outcomes
• Explain why build tools and source code should not remain in the final runtime image.
• Write and build a single-stage Dockerfile and a multi-stage Dockerfile.
• Copy only the compiled artifact from a builder stage into a smaller runtime stage.
• Run the application as a non-root user and verify the runtime identity.
• Compare Alpine, slim, distroless, and scratch base-image trade-offs.
• Document image sizes, tests, screenshots, and findings in a reproducible GitHub submission.